  "readme": "## README.md\n# Species Identification Dataset\n\nThis release contains a no-GSV multimodal tree species identification dataset organized around individual trees.\n\nRaw Google Street View images are not redistributed. Panorama IDs and related metadata are retained, and code is released separately to repopulate GSV imagery from those panorama IDs where users have appropriate API access and rights.\n\n## Contents\n\n- `tree_metadata.csv`: sanitized tree-level metadata.\n- `gsv_pano_ids.csv`: tree-level mapping to GSV panorama IDs and related capture/geometry fields.\n- `all_metadata.json`: sanitized nested metadata.\n- `instances_default.json`: annotation export.\n- `all_locations.csv`, `dataset_summary.json`, `dataset_and_labels_context.txt`: dataset context files.\n- `skysat_crops/`: one canonical RGB JPEG per example.\n- `sentinel1_pixel_timeseries/pixel_data/`: Sentinel-1 tree time series, one CSV per example.\n- `sentinel2_pixel_timeseries/pixel_data/`: Sentinel-2 tree time series, one CSV per example.\n- `planetscope_pixel_timeseries/pixel_data/`: PlanetScope tree time series, one CSV per example.\n- `species_classification_vectors_5full/`: full-modality species vector outputs.\n- `manifest/`: release manifests and audit files.\n- `sample_100/`: small reviewer-inspection sample with 100 complete examples across modalities.\n\n## Counts\n\n- Examples: 23,156 individual trees.\n- Raw Google Street View images included: no.\n- Modalities included: SkySat RGB crops, Sentinel-1 time series, Sentinel-2 time series, PlanetScope time series, and derived species-classification vectors.\n\n## Reproducibility\n\nThe release can be used without raw GSV images using the released remote-sensing modalities, labels, metadata, and vectors. Users who have appropriate API access and rights can use the retained panorama IDs with separately released code to repopulate GSV images through the provider-approved access path.\n\n## License\n\nThis dataset release is licensed under [Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/).\n\nUpstream and optional sources remain subject to their own terms: for example, Google Street View / Maps Platform rules if you fetch imagery from panorama IDs, Copernicus Sentinel and Planet policies for underlying satellite products, and any provider-specific restrictions noted in `croissant.json` provenance. The CC BY-NC license applies to this curated release as a whole; it does not override third-party licenses for data you obtain separately from those providers.\n",
